# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is local to this machine and never committed.
# Plain KEY=value lines: the Makefile includes this file directly, so no
# quotes and no spaces in paths.

# Directory with licensed IPs that cannot be committed, only if the product
# uses them: remove the #. Vivado scans it recursively for component.xml
# files.
# VIVADO_IP_REPO_EXT=/path/to/licensed/ip_repo

# Linux part (sw/), only if the product uses it: remove the # and set the
# checkouts of the sources, at the tags of sw/config.sh. build.sh checks the
# tags but never checks anything out.
# LINUX_SRC=/path/to/linux-xlnx
# UBOOT_SRC=/path/to/u-boot-xlnx
# Only for Vivado up to 2024.1:
# DT_XLNX_SRC=/path/to/device-tree-xlnx
# Kernel build directory, out/sw/linux if not set: for example to share one
# kernel build among products. Relative paths start from the product root.
# 'make linux-clean' deletes it only when it is inside out/sw/.
# LINUX_BUILD_DIR=/path/to/linux-build

# On Windows, if make cannot find vivado.bat by itself.
# VIVADO_BIN=vivado.bat
